app.main:app
│    │     │
│    │     └── variable: app = FastAPI()
│    │
│    └──────── module: main.py
│
└───────────── package: app/
Earlier you created a .venv, so use the Python inside that virtual environment.
source .venv/bin/activate
which python -> /ai-backend/.venv/bin/python
then run 
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload


install first time
python -m uvicorn app.main:app --reload
check
python -m pip show uvicorn
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Database:
PostgreSQL
│
├── database: ai_backend
│
└── user: ai_user
psql -h localhost -U ai_user -d ai_backend
CREATE USER ai_user WITH PASSWORD 'ai';
CREATE DATABASE ai_backend OWNER ai_user;

Engine
  ↓
database connectivity + connection pool

SessionLocal
  ↓
factory for SQLAlchemy sessions

Session
  ↓
unit used to query/change DB data

Base
  ↓
parent for ORM models
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Alembic
SQLAlchemy model
      ↓
Alembic migration
      ↓
PostgreSQL

alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add product description"
alembic upgrade head
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LLM
→ generates/understands natural-language responses

Embedding model
→ converts information into vectors

pgvector
→ stores/searches those vectors

sql -> In pgvector, <=> is the cosine distance operator.
SQLAlchemy -> Product.embedding.cosine_distance(query_embedding)

| Metric                    | pgvector operator   | SQLAlchemy            |

| Euclidean / L2 distance      | <->              | l2_distance()       |
| Negative inner product  	 | <#>             | max_inner_product() |
| Cosine distance      	 | <=>             | cosine_distance()   |

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
install pgvector in python directory of project
python -m pip install pgvector
